WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.150
- [Mark] All right, David.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.010
David, where are you from
originally? Where'd you grow up?

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:10.990
- [David] Reserve, New Mexico.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.290
- [Mark] New Mexico?
- [David] Yes.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.570
- [Mark] And tell me about your family.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.930
You grew up with both of your parents?

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.940
- I grew up with adopted parents

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.940
and I lived in a small village
in the middle of the forest.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.483
Everything is far away.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.273
But as I grew up,

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.900
I had a very, very troubled experience.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.233
- [Mark] What happened?

00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:34.910
- When I was little, my
parents used to neglect me

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.610
and leave me inside the room with nothing

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:38.913
and I didn't eat at all.

00:00:45.131 --> 00:00:48.910
I used to drink piss out
the bottle to survive.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:53.373
My dad hit me with a board,
like that, metal on the back.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.270
I started getting in and out
of jail at the age of 13,

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:00.823
all the way to the age of 17,

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.210
because I couldn't
really deal with the pain

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.960
and the abuse that I was
going through with my parents.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.410
When I was 17 then I
started striving to look

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.513
for my adopted, or my biological mother.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.960
When I found her, I was with her a week,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.710
caught her doing heroin in the room

00:01:22.002 --> 00:01:23.000
and she kicked me out in the streets

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.000
and I've been homeless for seven months.

00:01:29.657 --> 00:01:31.750
When I was a little kid, it was hard,

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.320
especially for me because I
grew up out in the country,

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:36.770
I didn't grow up in the city.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:43.493
But you know, I started trying
to change my life around.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:50.330
I still have the memories,
but I try to move on.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:51.840
- [Mark] How old are you?

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.440
- 18.
- [Mark] You're 18?

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.810
- Yeah, 18 and a half.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.020
I've been on the streets for seven months.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.030
- [Mark] So you were staying
with your mom recently?

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:00.863
Your real, biological mom?

00:02:00.863 --> 00:02:02.940
- I got off a year's probation,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:06.760
I stayed with my grandmother in Oklahoma

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:13.330
and I caught a Greyhound out
from Oklahoma to New Mexico

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.090
because I'd moved from New Mexico to there

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:18.240
when I got out of jail.

00:02:20.357 --> 00:02:22.150
I was with my mother for one week.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.840
Ever since then, I've been homeless.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:25.893
So I hitchhiked.

00:02:27.724 --> 00:02:30.330
I hitchhiked all the way
from Reserve, Mexico to here.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.540
But when I went back out to Oklahoma

00:02:37.697 --> 00:02:41.150
after my mother had
kicked me out, I, you know

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:42.210
went back to Oklahoma

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.740
and my grandmother was, you
know, trying to explain to me,

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:51.220
like, I know you've had a
troubled past and stuff like that,

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.063
but move on.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:58.863
So of course I came out here
to Los Angeles for the dream,

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.363
but I still go every day.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:06.790
- [Mark] To where?

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.760
- Just trying to hang in there.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:10.815
- [Mark] Oh, I see.

00:03:10.815 --> 00:03:13.183
Are you using any of the
drugs that are out here?

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:17.373
- Recently, I'm not gonna lie, yes.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:21.573
I've done drugs quite a bit,

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.170
but I'm trying to mellow
myself away from it.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.620
- [Mark] What drugs have you used?

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:28.803
- Popped xannies.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.000
Used to pop like, three of them at a time.

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:37.763
I smoke weed because it helps me out.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.870
Yeah, I'm kind of a drinker, but...

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.033
And I try to stay away from
meth and heroin, if anything,

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:53.573
but yeah, I have done meth
and overdone it, that's why.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.660
- [Mark] What are you doing for money now?

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.130
- [David] Right now I'm
pretty much stranded

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.080
at a point where I can't make anything.

00:04:03.813 --> 00:04:06.513
I've went around to places around here.

00:04:09.062 --> 00:04:11.720
Here's two things, either
I go back to my home state

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.260
or I stay here and try to make a living

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.410
out here in California.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.570
I don't want to end up like,

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.910
to the point where I'm dirty 24/7,

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.290
so I try to keep myself clean as possible.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.953
I get any showers I can
take, any clothes I can get.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.190
I do what I can do.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.040
- [Mark] Where do you sleep now?

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.180
- [David] I sleep anywhere
I can find that's clean.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:37.572
Not shit and pissed on--

00:04:37.572 --> 00:04:40.040
- [Mark] You don't have a tent?

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.090
- [David] I don't have a tent.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.600
I don't have any equipment.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.120
The only stuff I have is this right here.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.040
- [Mark] Your backpack?

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:47.873
- [David] Yup.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.770
- [Mark] It's a big backpack.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:55.200
- [David] Yup, I had 260
pounds in that before.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.033
- [Mark] Wow.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.459
So your relationship with your
foster parents is not great?

00:05:02.459 --> 00:05:04.600
- [David] It never really was great.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.960
It was one day, they're cool,

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.823
the next day they're pissed off.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:12.210
And my mother, when my
mother got pissed off,

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.613
she used to throw knives
over the counter top at me.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:17.950
- [Mark] And they were doing drugs or--

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.580
- No, my dad worked in Freeport McMoRan

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.550
in Morenci for 21 years.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:27.373
He'd come home from work, beat
the shit out of me, and then,

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.183
yeah.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.780
- [Mark] So your relationship
with your biological mom

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.803
is no better, right?

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.610
- Well, my biological mom,

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.280
I haven't gotten to know her that well,

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:46.490
she kicked me out after
one week of knowing her.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:49.820
My adopted mother is now
trying to convince me

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.910
of all kinds of stuff, and, you know,

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.290
it's kind of hard to trust her

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.750
after the stuff that I
went through for years,

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.053
since the age of six.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.250
- [Mark] did you finish high school?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.620
- No, I was pulled out at
ninth grade by my parents.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.770
There was a lawsuit against the school

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.560
because my dad was trying
to make millions off of

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:13.993
suing the school.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.063
He was using me as an advantage.

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:22.373
- [Mark] So do you have an ID at least?

00:06:22.373 --> 00:06:24.650
- I don't have an ID,
don't have social security,

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.300
all that's been stolen.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.370
That's why I went around
with all my stuff,

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.430
I try to keep an eye on it.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:33.390
Because out here people's
already jacked stuff from me.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:35.800
- [Mark] That happens everyday here.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:36.633
- Yeah.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:43.620
- [Mark] Do you have siblings or anything?

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:47.430
- I got a few left, but I
don't see them that much.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:52.310
I got one friend that I call
a true friend just because

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:56.253
he helped me out recently
when I was in New Mexico.

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:03.230
But you know, I've hitchhiked
7,000 miles this year, total.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.423
Or 2019 anyways.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:13.863
You know, I'm young, but I've
gotten to the point where,

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:17.790
you know, I did a lot of
drugs and alcohol in my teens,

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:18.740
when I was a minor.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.890
Now that I'm getting older, it just

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.860
feels like it's getting too old,

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:27.260
like I don't really want to, you know

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:29.160
mess with that stuff anymore.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.160
So I've been trying to keep
myself a little bit sober

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.363
off of a lot of it, just smoke weed.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:39.940
The reason why I smoke weed
'cause I have serious PTSD.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:42.710
My PTSD

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:49.150
flashbacks will come
in when I see something

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:51.597
that reminds me of something
that happened to me.

00:07:51.597 --> 00:07:53.290
- [Mark] What kind of
stuff happened to you

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:56.053
in your childhood that
was the most traumatic?

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.973
- The most traumatic was
when I was little, my mother,

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:04.110
when I was taking a bath, she would

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:08.070
chase me around the house naked and then

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.270
beat the shit out of me.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.920
She used to call my dad and
tell him all kinds of stuff

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.370
and he would come home and...

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.230
It was hell with him.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:29.230
It was a lot more complicated
than most families.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.783
When you talk abuse,
my dad used his fists.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:39.040
I got so used to it,
I'm not scared of dying,

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.790
I'm not scared of fighting anymore.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.120
So I'm hoping that I could get my GED

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:49.093
and just kind of get a job.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.043
You know what I mean?

00:08:51.043 --> 00:08:53.430
I've been broke, I've been
broke for a long time.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:54.730
- [Mark] That would be a great plan.

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:59.030
So, you know, I appreciate
you wanting to hear something,

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:03.890
but you know, everything
I'm telling you is the truth

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:08.313
because the stuff that
I went through is bad.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:12.490
And there's some stuff that I
don't want to say on camera,

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.430
if you know what I mean.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:17.030
And I'll kind of give
whoever's watching this a hint

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:19.790
about how bad it was.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:22.783
And yes, I have been bull whipped.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.250
I've been bull whipped.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:32.760
That is one of the most
painfullest, painfullest

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:34.440
thing that can happen to you.

00:09:38.501 --> 00:09:43.330
- [Mark] This is about
your adopted parents?

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:47.950
- My adopted father used to
take a bullwhip, (hisses)

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:50.740
go around me like that,
it wrapped around me

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.740
and slapped me in the chest really hard.

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:57.770
It was so painful I felt
like I was about to just...

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:08.300
These days when I wreck
or if I break my arm

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:11.143
or whatever I do, I broke my
wrist about two months ago,

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:16.763
I kinda like, tolerate the
pain because I'm so used to it.

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:19.723
- [Mark] Well good luck with everything,

00:10:19.723 --> 00:10:22.100
and try to steer clear of all the drugs.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:22.933
- Yes, sir.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:25.923
Thank you.
- [Mark] Thank you.

